// A `@target(.X)` is always a BODY, never a declaration. Without a bare
// `@target` of the same name to carry the signature, the `export` and the
// vaderdoc, telling a body from a declaration would mean looking elsewhere in
// the module — the one non-local question the model exists to avoid.

module "main"

@target(.Linux)
orphan :: fn() -> i32 = 1

main :: fn() -> i32 = 0
